WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
Bloom's Taxonomy is a toolbox that
teachers or students can use to classify

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.410
and organize learning objectives. It's
most popular version is based on the

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:14.490
cognitive domain and assumes that
learning should be structured from easy

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:23.300
to difficult in the following six steps:
One: remember. Two: understand. Three: apply.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:34.410
Four: analyze. Five evaluate. Six: create On
the first level we learn to remember.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:39.360
There is just rote memorization and
recollection of facts without much

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.640
understanding, for example if we learn
about lemons we want to remember the

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.500
name, shape, color, size and that they are
sour

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.719
once we memorise these essentially
meaningless facts we move to the second

00:00:54.719 --> 00:01:02.430
level of learning. On level two we learn
to understand. We begin to decode

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:07.049
information and learn that a lemon is
yellow when it's ripe to eat and if we

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:12.330
take a bite that it's really super sour,
we also understand that lemons love

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:17.330
sunshine and that they contain lots of
vitamin C which is a great natural

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:23.280
antioxidant that keeps us healthy. Now as
we really understand a lemon we can work

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:30.720
with it. On the third level we apply what
we know. We've understood that while

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:36.119
lemons are sour they are also a great
provider of vitamin C. To apply this

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:40.950
knowledge in a meaningful way we could
boil a lemon into hot water and add some

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:48.229
honey, then serve this hot lemon to our
sick sister who's in need of treatment.

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:54.189
On the 4th level we learn to analyse,
this involves examining and breaking

00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:58.750
down information into components
determining how the parts relate to one

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:04.799
another and finding evidence to support
generalisations. We study the lemon flesh,

00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:10.209
examine the skin and look at levels of
vitamins. We conclude that we can eat

00:02:10.209 --> 00:02:15.250
everything inside while the skin tastes
bitter and contains traces of toxic

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:20.160
pesticides it ought not to be consumed.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:27.579
Now we are ready to evaluate, we analyse,
critique and compare. To evaluate our

00:02:27.579 --> 00:02:31.959
lemon as a good source of vitamins we
compare it to other sources such as

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:36.840
oranges and supplements. We look at the
following properties: vitamin levels,

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:43.480
affordability, taste and packaging waste.
If we evaluate our thoughts critically

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:48.549
and without bias we learn where the
lemons score high and where others score

00:02:48.549 --> 00:02:56.170
higher. Now after we have learned,
understood. applied, analysed and

00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:03.370
evaluated, we are ready to create. As we
now really understand lemons also in

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.930
comparison to similar things we can
formulate a plan to create our own

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:14.799
natural lemonate. It's now easy to come
up with a cute shop design a good name

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:20.459
and a good slogan: "natural, healthy, yummy"

00:03:20.579 --> 00:03:27.400
Bloom's Taxonomy was first created in
1946 by American psychologist Benjamin

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:33.549
Bloom. The revised version from 2001, as
just presented, serves as the backbone of

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:38.680
many teaching philosophies in particular
those that aim towards teaching specific

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:44.349
skills. Each level usually comes with a
clear learning objective that can be

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:49.680
tested. Critics of the taxonomy often
questioned the existence of a sequential

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:55.030
hierarchical link between each level.
What are your thoughts? Please share them

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:59.679
in the comments below

